<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        ElegoMotors — company address wrapping fix (affects every PDF)

        web.external_layout_standard puts the company's own address in a
        <div class="col-6" name="company_address"> inside a <div class="row">
        with nothing else sharing that row — half the page width sits empty
        next to it for no reason. With ElegoMotors' compound Indian address
        (street/street2/city/state/zip each reasonably long on their own),
        that half-width column forces awkward wrapping, confirmed live on
        staging1 across multiple PDF types (Delivery Slip, Purchase Order) —
        this is the actual root cause of what was reported as address text
        "overlapping" other content. Confirmed the address DATA itself is
        already correctly split across the proper fields (Settings >
        Companies), so this needed a template fix, not a data fix.

        Widening to full width (col-12) gives the same content much more
        room to lay out cleanly, with no competing content lost since the
        row had nothing else in it. This is company_id=1's report layout
        (web.external_layout_standard, confirmed via
        company.external_report_layout_id.key on staging1) — affects every
        report using the shared header, which is the intended fix per the
        user's report that this shows up "around every PDF section".
    -->

    <template id="external_layout_standard_ego" inherit_id="web.external_layout_standard">

        <xpath expr="//div[@name='company_address']" position="attributes">
            <attribute name="class">col-12</attribute>
        </xpath>

    </template>

</odoo>
